# These patterns are matched with filepath.Match, in which a single * never
# crosses a directory separator: an unprefixed pattern excludes only what sits
# at the root of the build context. Anything that must be kept out wherever it
# appears is written with the **/ prefix, which does span directories.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
.git
.gitattributes
.gitignore
**/.env
**/.env.*
venv/
env/
.venv/
*.log
logs/
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.yaml
docker-compose.example.yml
# Backups of the local compose file carry the same credentials it does, and
# .gitignore already keeps them out of the repository. The entries above do not
# cover them, because there is no implicit prefix matching here either: a name
# that merely begins with docker-compose.yml is not excluded by it. Without
# these three lines COPY . . places a file full of live credentials inside a
# published image, where docker history or docker save will hand it to anyone.
**/docker-compose.*.bak-*
**/*.bak
**/*.bak-*
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
README.md
README_CN.md
README_JP.md
README_FA.md
doc/
*.pdf
**/*.pdf
docs/
tests/
pytest.ini
.pytest_cache/
requirements-dev.txt
# Local working notes, untracked and not part of the software.
.superpowers/
# LICENSE is deliberately not excluded. MIT requires the notice to travel with
# substantial portions of the software, and publishing an image is a
# distribution of it.
.github/
